  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender-responsive programmes to promote gender equality, decent working conditions and equal opportunities in world of work developed and implemented</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Turkiye is a ratifying country to C100 and C111. ILO is implementing the &#x201c;More and Better Jobs for Women&#x201d; Programme, financed by Sweden in cooperation with the workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; organizations, public agencies, private sector, academia and CSO&#x2019;s since January 2019. Objective of the Programme is to increase the number of women working with decent conditions in line with ILS focusing on gender equality. ILO has also intensified activities to ensure equal opportunities and treatment and address stigma and negative stereotypes for persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
